# mano-android-use agent rule

When controlling Android via this repo's MCP (`mano-android-use` / `mau`):

**Principle:** Host picks goal/plan; mau orchestrates; Grounder sees screenshots; L0 executes.

1. Start with `ready` (or `doctor` then `ready`). Honor `tips[]`, `screen.awake`, `text_backend.available`.
2. **Default multi-step path:** `android_run` or `android_run_plan` (with `package=` warm-ensure when known; `launch_app` / `cold_start=true` only for true relaunch). Do **not** open installed apps by typing Chinese in a browser. MCP defaults are short (`max_steps≈10`, ~90s soft budget). **Every** run returns `task_patch` + ResumeSpec (`resume`/`continue_hint`): merge `task_patch` into Host TaskState (OR-merge `progress`; replace `resume`/`screen_digest`); on resume fill `do.*` (`omit_package`, `cold_start=false`, keep `tree_hints`/`success_check`) and pass `progress_json` from TaskState; honor `dont[]` (**no HOME / force_stop / rewrite_goal / propose_action loop**). Prefer `tree_hints` or「quoted」labels when the target is a stable a11y string so mau can tree-shortcut before VLM.
3. **Goals:** never put payment/submit button copy in the goal (e.g. avoid「立即支付」); say stop-before-pay instead. Meituan-class flows → short staged goals (搜 / 规格加购 / 可选凑单) via `android_run_plan` or several short `android_run`s — not one giant goal.
4. Do **not** drive multi-step goals with `propose_action` chains or `propose_action(execute=true)` (deprecated). Use L0 `tap`/`swipe`/`type_text`/`press_button` only for install dialogs, one-off correction, or debug. Unchanged screens are handled inside `android_run` (skip VLM → recover → STUCK); after `type`/`click`/`swipe`, a short act grace skips BACK.
5. Chinese `type_text` only if AdbKeyboard is available; otherwise tap/launch only and tell the user to install OpenATX AdbKeyboard.
6. APK install / ColorOS「继续安装」dialogs: handle with `observe`+`tap` or ask the human — not as an `android_run` goal.
7. If the screen is off, wake/unlock first; `android_run` only tries one `KEYCODE_WAKEUP`.
8. On `NEED_HUMAN` / `BLOCKED_BY_POLICY` for payment UI, stop.
9. Wireless ADB: if connect fails, re-pair/connect and refresh `MANO_DEVICE_SERIAL` (ports change). Prefer MCP L0 over shell `adb input tap` so safety + journal apply.
10. After every `android_run` / `android_run_plan`, **tell the user the cost**: quote `cost_report.narrative` (or summarize totals). Explain who spent time — `observe` (ADB tree/screenshot), `grounder` (VLM, also all tokens), `act` (tap/type/swipe). For plans, also list each stage’s `total_ms` / tokens / `dominant_phase`. When resuming, also surface `progress` / `resume.do` briefly so the user sees why the next short run is safe (no cold start).

